  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving West African Chimpanzee Conservation through Protected Area Management in the Grabo National Park</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to protect chimpanzees in the proposed Grebo National Park by improving management capacity of chimpanzees and developing local community involvement in chimpanzee conservation. The recipient will re-train FDA agents and local community members in biomonitoring (data collection); implement and supervise biomonitoring missions of FDA and community led teams collecting data on chimpanzees and anthropogenic threats, train and support FDA in biomonitoring data analysis and report preparation, re-train local community jmembers to act as eco-guards for the PGNP; carry out a sensitization on the status of the PGNP; create and support micro-projects of alternative protein sources in local communities.</narrative>
  </description>
